{
  "_doc": "The world map (docs/PHASE4_DESIGN.md), in pages of two chapters (docs/PHASE8_CHAPTER3_4.md 第 1 部 §3; page 3, chapters 5 and 6: docs/PHASE9_CHAPTER5_6.md 第 1 部 §3): a chapter's `page` is where its islands are; `pages[].title` is the heading beside \"ちず\" once there is more than one page. Islands are placed in % of the map area (x from the left, y from the top) of their page. An island without a stage file yet is shown as a '?' silhouette (no name, no records, it only wiggles); the rails to it are laid as usual, so a page can come before its stages, and the island gets its name once its stage file is there (and its own picture once it has a `diorama`). `diorama` is what scripts/render-map.mjs puts on the island to draw public/map/<id>.png: models (bottom centre on the island top, y = 0), at [x, z] m, rotY in degrees. `chapters[].finale` plays once when its link is first drawn, or without a link once the chapter is done (a light — gold round a `ring`, water along a `path`, or an aurora — then a card); `chapters[].teaser` is a later chapter's single \"?\" island on the page of its `from` island (docs/PHASE7_FINISH.md §3). A link's optional `via` is the curve's control point in %; `afterChapter` holds it back until that chapter is done; `exit`/`enter` take it to another page through the cloud gate (the gate's place on each page, with the curve to it).",
